One thing I noticed is that you mentioned that browser wording (browse, in the browser) runs the loop on free sources with the soul planning each step and the browser gate on every step. [NOT VERIFIED] I found a mention of this in `server/cloudflare/office_router.js` (line 123) where it says: [NOT VERIFIED] ```javascript
if (type === 'browser') {
  // For 'browser' type, we run the loop on free sources with the soul planning each step
  // and the browser gate on every step.
  const soul = brain.soul();
  const browserGate = browserGateFactory(soul);
  const loop = new AgentLoop({
    // ...
  });
  loop.addStep(browserGate);
  // ...
}
```

This suggests that the `browser` type indeed runs the loop with the soul planning each step and the browser gate on every step.

[NOT VERIFIED] Regarding the routing of answers, I found a mention of this in `server/cloudflare/agent_permissions.js` (line 456) where it says: [NOT VERIFIED] ```javascript
if (type === 'study') {
  // For 'study' type, we route to REA.
  return 'REA';
} else if (type === 'story') {
  // For 'story' type, we route to Mira.
